    description: "WHAT\ncpp.py _alternatives_of_one_function compares parameter TYPES only. Since PR #2370 a parameter's pointer, reference and array marks are in meta[\"parameters\"][i][\"declarator\"], and this check does not read them: two overloads in one file that differ only by marks (f(int) / f(int*)) are treated as #if alternatives of one function, so a call to either is resolved at confidence 1.0, not ambiguous, and one constructor edge is drawn.\n\nREPRO\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v20_11242026/cfamily/RESULTS.md, \"Not fixed\" 1 (cfamily agent; left alone because it is call resolution, not identity).\n\nNOT CHECKED\nThe fixture's edges were not re-run by the filing agent.\n\nFound 2026-11-24 while building PR #2370 (stable-id v20). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v20_11242026/STATUS.md and the package RESULTS.md named above."  # 7cd6
